# Story Workflow

- Each component story lives in `src/stories/<ComponentName>/<ComponentName>.stories.tsx`.
- Import library entities in stories from `@components/<ComponentName>` (path alias to `src/components/<ComponentName>`).
- Story meta baseline:
  - `title: "Components/<ComponentName>"`
  - `component: <ComponentName>`
  - `tags: ["autodocs"]`
  - useful `parameters.docs`, `argTypes`, and default `args`.
- Do not use inline styles in story markup (`style={{ ... }}` in render/demo layouts).
- If custom story layout styling is needed:
  - create `src/stories/<ComponentName>/<ComponentName>Stories.module.scss`;
  - import it as CSS Modules and apply classes in JSX.
- Reuse project-level Storybook decorators from `.storybook/preview.tsx`; add local decorators only when necessary.
- If a component is added or its public API is changed in `src/components/**`, updating the corresponding story is mandatory.
- Story updates must reflect real current API and behavior, including new/removed/renamed props and changed states.
